---
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { products, productUrl } from '../lib/catalog';
const sheets = products.filter((p) => p.datasheet).sort((a, b) => a.sku.localeCompare(b.sku));
---
<Base title="Support" description="How to choose a rack: rack units, width, depth and load. Plus LDR datasheets and answers to common questions.">
  <div class="wrap support">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={url('/')}>Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>Support</nav>
    <header class="page-intro">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Sizing guidance, datasheets and answers to common questions.</p>
      <nav class="jump" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#choosing">Choosing a rack</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#downloads">Datasheets</a><a href="#warranty">Warranty & returns</a></nav>
    </header>

    <section id="choosing" class="block">
      <h2>Choosing a rack</h2>
      <div class="guide">
        <article>
          <h3>1. Height in rack units (U)</h3>
          <p>One rack unit is 44.45 mm (1.75"). Add up the U of everything you'll mount: most switches and patch panels are 1U, small servers 1–2U, rack UPSs 2U. Desktop boxes like an NBN modem or small NVR sit on a shelf, so allow about 2U for each shelf. Then add 25% or more for growth.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>2. Depth</h3>
          <p>Cabinet depth is quoted as an external measurement. What matters is the <strong>usable mounting depth</strong> between the front and rear rails, listed on each product page. It should exceed your deepest device plus room for power and patch leads at the back (allow around 100 mm).</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>3. Wall or floor</h3>
          <p>Wall cabinets (4U–18U) keep network gear off the floor in offices, retail and CCTV installs. Choose a floor cabinet for servers, UPS batteries or anything over 18U. Check the wall can carry the loaded cabinet's weight.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>4. Width, doors and airflow</h3>
          <p>600 mm wide suits most installs. 800 mm wide cabinets give room for vertical cable managers and dense patching. Glass doors let you see status lights; mesh doors move more air for servers and switches running hot.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-line"><a class="btn btn--primary" href={url('/rack-builder')}>Let the Rack Builder size it for you</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="faq" class="block">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details><summary>Can I buy LDR directly?</summary><p>LDR is sold through resellers and integrators and supplied by Leader Systems. See <a href={url('/where-to-buy')}>Where to buy</a>, or request a quote and we'll pass it to a reseller near you.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will 19" equipment fit a 10" mini rack?</summary><p>No. 10" mini racks take 10-inch equipment only. For standard 19" switches and patch panels, use a wall cabinet.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What's the difference between the Carbon range and the existing LDR range?</summary><p>Carbon is the new generation, with a charcoal finish and a wider choice of sizes and fit-out parts, including spare doors, plinths and vertical cable managers. The existing LDR range stays available. Where both ranges offer the same size, product pages link to the equivalent.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do floor cabinets include a PDU and shelves?</summary><p>Some do. The LDR 18U, 22U and 42U floor cabinets include an 8-port PDU, a 4-way fan and two fixed shelves. Check "In the box" on each product page.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Are LDR accessories compatible with other brands' racks?</summary><p>Most LDR accessories follow the 19" standard and fit any standard 19" rack. Shelf depth needs to suit the rack's depth: each shelf page lists the cabinet depths it's recommended for.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section id="downloads" class="block">
      <h2>Datasheets</h2>
      <p class="muted">Datasheets for the Carbon range will be published here as they're released.</p>
      <ul class="sheets">
        {sheets.map((p) => (
          <li><a href={p.datasheet!} rel="noopener">{p.name}</a><span class="sku">{p.sku}</span><a href={productUrl(p)} class="muted">Product page</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="warranty" class="block">
      <h2>Warranty & returns</h2>
      <p>LDR products carry a manufacturer's warranty, listed on each product page (12 months for the current range). Warranty claims and returns go through the reseller you bought from, who will lodge them with Leader Systems.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .support { padding-bottom: 80px; }
  .page-intro { padding: 18px 0 8px; }
  .page-intro h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.25rem); }
  .jump { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 18px; }
  .jump a { text-decoration: none; background: var(--paper-2); border-radius: 999px; padding: 8px 16px; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 500; transition: background .2s; }
  .jump a:hover { background: var(--paper-3); }
  .block { padding: 40px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 24px; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .guide { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 420px), 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  .guide article { background: var(--paper-2); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .guide p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .cta-line { margin-top: 24px; }
  details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 4px 0; max-width: 820px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 12px 0; font-weight: 600; }
  details p { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .sheets { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 16px 0 0; columns: 2 380px; column-gap: 32px; }
  .sheets li { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: baseline; padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); break-inside: avoid; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sheets li a:first-child { font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .sheets li a:first-child:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .sheets li .muted { margin-left: auto; font-size: .8125rem; }
</style>
